WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.278 --> 00:00:02.820
ALICIA WILLIAMS:
Today, we're talking

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:08.039
about Tau VMs, data ingestion,
and AppSheet in Gmail.

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:10.620
I'm Alicia, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.860
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.260
In June, we announced a
new virtual machine family,

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.210
Tau VMs, that extends
Compute Engine's VM offerings

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.430
with an option that
delivers the best price

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.150
performance among leading
clouds for scale-out workloads.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.310
The first member of
the Tau VM family,

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.850
T2D, is now
available in preview.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.830
This week, we're
excited to share

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.480
the results of
independent testing

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.140
by Phoronix, validating Google's
claims on price performance

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.070
leadership.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.920
Check out the blog for more.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.740
Developing cloud-based
data ingestion pipelines

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.960
that replicate data
from various sources

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.150
into your cloud
data warehouse can

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.400
be a massive undertaking
that requires

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.440
significant investment.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.440
We have defined principles
for data pipeline planning

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.060
to begin the process.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.300
These principles are intended
to help you answer key business

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.580
questions about your
effort and begin

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.530
to build data
pipelines that address

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.690
your business and
technical needs.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.300
AppSheet's new
capabilities within Gmail

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.350
are powerful because AppSheet
is a true no-code platform

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.620
and anyone can create one,
making it easier than ever

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.170
to translate a great
idea into software

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.980
and deploy it to teammates in
an easily consumable fashion.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.470
AppSheet apps can be
connected to the data source

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:31.110
of your choice, like a
Google Sheet, SQL database,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.310
or Salesforce.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.650
Imagine how useful
it'll be when creating

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.930
a dynamic email,
because you can update

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.240
data in any of these
sources without having

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.380
to leave your inbox.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.570
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.010
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:49.400
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.050
We'll see you in the cloud.

